ing weeks, or Askar converting his spending advantage into traction, could tip the race to either side.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 57 days old; polling uncertainty inflated."]}, "overview": "Florida's 22nd District is an open seat where a Republican-leaning map collides with a strongly favorable Democratic year. Casey Askar, who has raised $7.4 million and holds a large cash advantage, faces Pia Dandiya, a Democrat who has raised $4.6 million and drawn a Buttigieg campaign visit plus a cross-party endorsement from the Wellington mayor. Most race ratings call it a tossup, with a few outlets leaning Democratic and one tilting Republican.\n\nThe available polling is thin and dated, with Democratic-sponsored August surveys showing a dead heat, and the candidates have traded sharp attacks centered on corruption claims. Outside groups have directed spending against Askar while largely bypassing Dandiya. Prediction markets give Dandiya roughly a 60 percent chance, and the environment tilts the fundamentals her way, but Askar's money keeps this genuinely competitive.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.5161, "margin": 0.22}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.4293, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.5493, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.5402, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.4658, "margin": 0.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4995, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.5432, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.5455, "margin": 0.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.5764, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.5967, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.5933, "margin": 1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.5824, "margin": 0.8}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.5625, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.5006, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.4998, "margin": 0.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.56